# A PAD THROWS ITS SHADOW BEFORE IT COMES (19_colossi `_warn`, DESIGN 5c). The
# straddling walker is staged twenty world minutes before its foot comes down in
# this world's first tread, and the player stands on a pad's crater floor, under
# where the pad will come, looking down. A breath and a half before the foot is
# low enough to stop bodies, the ground the pad will cover is marked and darkens
# inside the mark, all the way down; then the pad puts the player out from under
# it, and lands where it said.
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=600 tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_warning.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0-20 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0
# From the shoulder, the foot itself coming down over the player:
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=600 tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_warning.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0-20 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0 --view=shoulder
zoom 34
await colossus_foot 30
near colossus_crater
mouse 0,-100 0.5
until colossus_warned 60
# From the shoulder the view tips up to what is coming (Shoulder.GAZE_LEAST);
# from above the mouse changes nothing.
mouse 0,-300 0.8
wait 0.3
shot 00-under-the-coming-foot with colossus_warned
wait 1.5
shot 01-darker-as-it-comes with colossus_warned
until colossus_blocks 20
wait 0.5
shot 02-put-out-from-under-it
until colossus_tread 60
wait 0.2
shot 03-it-lands-where-it-said
